UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Claude Code is Anthropic's AI coding agent, currently at CLI version 2.1.291 (October 2026), with Claude Opus 5.5 as the default model. It runs across the terminal, VS Code, JetBrains, a desktop app and the web, and can drive cloud agents, subagents and computer use.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'claude-code' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Claude Code is Anthropic's agentic coding tool. It reads your codebase, edits files, runs commands and can carry a task from a plain-language request through to a working change, rather than just suggesting completions in an editor.

The current release is CLI 2.1.291. The default model is now Claude Opus 5.5 across Pro, Max, Team, Enterprise and the Anthropic API. Opus 4.8 had previously been the default only on the API, Max, Team Premium and Enterprise pay-as-you-go tiers for a period before being superseded.

Beyond the terminal, Claude Code also runs as VS Code and JetBrains extensions, as a desktop app and on the web. It supports cloud agents, subagent orchestration, computer use, scheduled cloud agents (Routines), background subagents and an Auto mode available on Pro and on Bedrock, Google Cloud and Microsoft Foundry.

Pricing: the Free tier ($0) does not include Claude Code. It is bundled into Pro ($17/month billed annually or $20/month billed monthly), Max (from $100/month, billed monthly only, with a higher-usage tier also available), Team Standard ($20/seat/month billed annually or $25/seat/month billed monthly, for teams of 2 to 150) and Team Premium ($100/seat/month billed annually or $125/seat/month billed monthly). Enterprise is priced at $20/seat/month billed annually plus usage at API rates. Separate pay-as-you-go API pricing includes Opus 5.5 at $4/$20 per million input/output tokens, Sonnet 5.5 at $2/$10, and Haiku 4.5 at $1/$5; a faster mode for Opus 5.5 runs at roughly 2x standard pricing.

Limitations are worth knowing. There is no free way to use Claude Code, usage caps apply even on paid plans, and heavy agentic runs on the API can get expensive. High-effort agent runs can also be slow and consume tokens quickly.

It suits professional developers and teams who want an agent that actually edits and ships code, especially those already on a Claude Pro, Max or Team plan who want coding included without a separate API bill.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'claude-code' AND lang = 'en';

