UPDATE tools SET faq = $x$[{"q": "O que é o Claude Code?", "a": "Claude Code é o agente de codificação oficial da Anthropic. Ele lê sua base de código, escreve código, executa comandos, corrige bugs e completa tarefas multiarquivo de forma autônoma, funcionando no terminal, VS Code, JetBrains, em um aplicativo desktop ou na web."}, {"q": "Quanto custa o Claude Code?", "a": "O Claude Code está incluído nos planos Claude Pro (a partir de $17/mês com cobrança anual, $20/mês com cobrança mensal), Max (a partir de $100/mês), Team Standard, Team Premium e Enterprise. Nesses planos, o Claude Code compartilha o mesmo conjunto de uso dos seus chats com o Claude; o uso pay-as-you-go separado da API também está disponível através do Anthropic Console."}, {"q": "Qual a diferença entre Claude Code e Cursor?", "a": "O Claude Code também funciona como extensões para VS Code e JetBrains, como aplicativo desktop e na web, não apenas no terminal. Ele foi criado para desenvolvedores que querem um agente que lê, edita e executa código em todo o seu fluxo de trabalho, enquanto o Cursor é uma IDE completa construída sobre o VS Code com uma interface visual."}, {"q": "O que o Claude Code consegue fazer de forma autônoma?", "a": "O Claude Code consegue ler e editar arquivos, executar comandos de shell, rodar testes, pesquisar na base de código, gerenciar o git e completar tarefas de engenharia em várias etapas do início ao fim com o mínimo de instruções."}]$x$::jsonb
 WHERE slug = 'claude-code' AND lang = 'pt';

UPDATE tools SET best_for = $x$AI IDE, agentic coding, multi-repo, PR review, parallel agents$x$
 WHERE slug = 'cursor' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Cursor is an AI-first code editor built on VS Code with agentic coding, multi-repo support, parallel agents, and automated PR review. Its in-house model lineup now includes Grok 4.7, Grok 4.6, Grok 4.5, and Composer 2.5, alongside supported third-party models.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'cursor' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Cursor is an AI-first code editor that started as a VS Code fork and has grown into a full agentic coding platform. Instead of just autocompleting lines, it can plan and carry out multi-step changes across a repository, run its own review passes, and hand work off to background agents.

The current stable build is 3.23.23, as reported by Cursor's own update endpoint; the public changelog no longer shows version numbers. The major recent development is Cursor's acquisition by SpaceX, completed August 14, 2026, following an April 2026 training partnership. Cursor's in-house model line is now built around Grok (Grok 4.6 released August 2026, Grok 4.7 released September 2026), while Composer 2.5 remains available in the Cursor Models pool. Recent additions include Projects (beta), self-hosted machines, and Rollouts and Security Review bots for Teams and Enterprise customers.

Key capabilities include the Composer agent for large edits, cloud agents and cloud dev environments triggered with /in-cloud, automatic code review, and Bugbot for automated PR review. It still supports third-party models, MCP servers, custom rules, and hooks, so you are not locked into any single model family.

Pricing is tiered. Hobby is free, with no card required but limited Agent requests and Composer access. Pro (Individual) is $20 per month and includes a Cursor Models usage pool (Grok 4.7, Grok 4.6, Grok 4.5, Composer 2.5) plus an Other Models pool for third-party models billed at API price, along with unlimited Tab, Bugbot, and Cloud Agents. Pro Plus is $60 per month, aimed at daily agent users, and Ultra is $200 per month for power users. Teams has two seat types: Standard at $40 per user per month (SSO, team marketplace, Bugbot, privacy mode) and Premium at $120 per user per month (higher agent limits). Enterprise pricing is custom and includes pooled usage, invoicing, and SCIM. A lower-cost regional plan is also available in India, billed monthly in local currency, with a reduced feature set.

The main limitations are cost and complexity. The split between Cursor Models and Other Models usage pools, plus usage-based Bugbot billing on individual plans, can make costs hard to predict. Being a VS Code fork, it occasionally lags behind upstream extensions, and the most capable features assume you are comfortable letting an agent make sweeping changes.

Cursor suits developers who want an agent that can take on real multi-file tasks, not just suggest snippets. It is a strong fit for professional teams already living in VS Code, and less compelling for people who only want lightweight autocomplete or work in a non-VS-Code editor.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'cursor' AND lang = 'en';

