UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Remove.bg is a Canva-owned AI tool that automatically removes backgrounds from images. There is no public version number; it runs a proprietary background-removal engine offered through free low-resolution previews plus a credit-based model for full-resolution downloads.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'remove-bg' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Remove.bg is a specialized web service and API that isolates the subject of a photo and strips out the background in a single step. It is owned by Canva Austria GmbH and is aimed at people who need clean cutouts for product shots, portraits, and marketing graphics without opening an image editor.

There is no public version numbering, and nothing fundamental has changed recently. The tool still runs the same proprietary AI engine and keeps the long-standing structure of free previews, subscriptions, and pay-as-you-go credits. Ownership remains with Canva, and there has been no shift from free to paid or paid to free.

In practice you upload an image or paste a URL and get an automatic cutout in a few seconds. It handles hair, fur, and semi-transparent edges reasonably well, supports transparent PNG output, and offers a browser tool, desktop and mobile apps, an API, and integrations with tools like Photoshop and Figma.

Pricing is built around credits. A free account gives you low-resolution web previews capped at 0.25 MP, plus the first 50 API or app calls each month at no charge. Pay-as-you-go credits never expire; per-image cost ranges from about $1.00 on the smallest 3-credit pack down to roughly $0.21 on the largest 8,000-credit pack. Subscription plans can be billed monthly or at a lower per-month rate if paid annually, and subscription credits are valid only within their billing month with no rollover: the Personal tier is $9 per month billed monthly, or $8.10 per month billed yearly, for 40 credits; Professional plans range from 200 credits at $39 per month billed monthly (or $35.10 per month billed yearly) up to 5,000 credits at $589 per month billed monthly (or $530.10 per month billed yearly); and Business plans scale further, up to 75,000 credits at $5,450 per month billed monthly (or $4,905 per month billed yearly).

The main limitation is that the free tier is genuinely a preview: downloads are capped at 0.25 MP, so any full-resolution result requires paid credits. Complex edges, busy backgrounds, and low-contrast subjects can still need manual touch-ups, and pay-as-you-go pricing is expensive for small batches even though it improves at volume.

Remove.bg suits e-commerce sellers, marketers, and designers who need fast, consistent cutouts at scale and are comfortable paying per image or by subscription for full-resolution output.$x$
