UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Claude Design is Anthropic's design assistant, included only in paid Claude plans, that turns a team's codebase and design files into a reusable design system. It launched on April 17, 2026 as a research preview running on the Claude Opus 4.7 vision model.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'claude-design' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Claude Design is a design-focused feature from Anthropic, bundled into paid Claude subscriptions rather than sold as a standalone product. It is aimed at turning a team's existing codebase and design files into polished, consistent design output.

It launched on April 17, 2026 as a research preview from Anthropic Labs, running on the Claude Opus 4.7 vision model. Anthropic's current product page no longer uses the 'research preview' label and does not name an underlying model, so its present status and the model powering it are unconfirmed.

The core idea is that Claude Design reads a team's codebase and design files and uses them to auto-build a reusable design system. It exports finished work to PPTX, PDF or HTML, can send output directly to connected tools including Adobe, Canva, Gamma, Lovable, Miro, Replit, Vercel and Wix, and can hand off to Claude Code for implementation. For Team and Enterprise accounts, an admin must enable the feature in Organization settings.

There is no standalone price. Access is included with paid Claude plans and metered against each plan's usage limits: Pro at $20/month ($17/month billed annually), Max plans starting from $100/month, Team Standard at $25/seat/month ($20/seat/month billed annually), Team Premium at $125/seat/month ($100/seat/month billed annually), and Enterprise at $20/seat/month billed annually plus usage charged at API rates. The Free $0 plan does not include Claude Design.

Usage counts against your subscription's own limits, with the option to buy extra usage if you go beyond them. As a feature that has already changed since its original research-preview launch, its capabilities and availability may continue to shift.

It suits product teams and designers already on a paid Claude plan who want to generate a consistent design system from existing code and files, and who value exporting to common formats or handing off to Claude Code.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'claude-design' AND lang = 'en';

