UPDATE tools SET description = $x$DeepL is a translation service built on its own specialized translation LLM, covering 100+ languages for text and offering a separate real-time voice-to-voice mode. It has a free plan plus paid Individual, Team, Business, and Enterprise tiers billed per user.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'deepl' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$DeepL is a machine-translation service known for producing natural, context-aware output rather than word-for-word conversions. It handles text and full documents, integrates into browsers and desktop apps, and includes DeepL Write, a separate assistant for rephrasing and polishing text.

DeepL now runs its own specialized translation LLM rather than relying only on generic models, and the service states it covers 100+ languages for text translation. It also offers DeepL Voice, a real-time voice-to-voice translation feature for meetings and conversations that supports 40+ languages; a limited number of voice minutes is included on paid plans.

Capabilities span quick text translation, whole-document translation that preserves formatting, glossaries and tone controls, the Write assistant for rephrasing, and an API for developers who want translation inside their own products.

Pricing is tiered. The Free plan gives 50,000 characters per month, one file translation per month (up to 5MB), and one glossary. Individual (Pro) raises the character allowance to 300,000 per month, adds full-page translation and a handful of files per month, plus some included voice minutes, billed per month on an annual plan. Team is priced per user per month on an annual plan and adds a much larger character allowance, bulk file translation, multiple glossaries, and SSO on larger teams. Business, also billed per user per month annually, offers unlimited characters, more files per month, unlimited glossaries, translation memory, and includes Write Pro. Enterprise pricing is custom. DeepL advertises a discount for annual versus monthly billing, though monthly list prices are not published on its pricing page. API pricing is handled on a separate page and was not verified.

Limitations include tight character and file caps on the free plan for regular work, Write Pro being confirmed as included only on the Business tier, and rarer language pairs likely still lagging the largest general-purpose translation models. Per-user Team and Business pricing can also add up for larger groups, and exact monthly-billed and API prices are not confirmed from DeepL's public pages.

DeepL suits people and teams who translate regularly and care about output that reads naturally: professional translators, localization teams, and businesses handling multilingual documents and customer communication.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'deepl' AND lang = 'en';

