UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Lindy is an AI agent-building platform now positioned as an 'AI teammate,' with a per-user Team plan starting at $29.99/month for 3,000 credits and a custom Enterprise tier. There is no public version number, and it offers a 7-day free trial with $50 in credits rather than an ongoing free plan.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'lindy' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Lindy is a platform for building and running AI agents that act on your behalf. It ships continuously rather than exposing numbered releases, so there is no public version number to track.

The platform recently repositioned itself around the message 'The AI Teammate That Lets You Do More.' The old consumer-facing Plus, Pro and Max tiers are gone, replaced by a simpler structure: a free trial, a per-user Team plan, and a custom Enterprise tier. Lindy now advertises connections to 1,000+ tools plus MCP servers, alongside email, calendar, iMessage/SMS and meeting-note integrations.

On capability, Lindy can chain its integrations into multi-step automations, and its pricing page lists model selection (choosing among underlying frontier LLMs from third-party vendors) and computer use, which lets agents operate a browser and interact with apps that lack a clean API, as part of the Team plan. Lindy's own homepage separately describes computer use as available 'Pro tier and up,' a label that no longer appears in the current pricing structure, so it's unclear exactly which Team tier unlocks it.

Pricing starts with a 7-day free trial that includes $50 in credits and requires no credit card. After the trial, the Team plan bills per active user per month on a credit basis, starting at $29.99/month for 3,000 credits and scaling up through published tiers (for example $49.99 for 5,000 credits, $99.99 for 15,000 credits) up to $9,999.50/month for 1,750,000 credits. Additional credits can be topped up at $10 per 1,000, the same rate as the base plans. Enterprise is custom-priced and adds SSO, SCIM, HIPAA with a signed BAA, audit logs and dedicated support. No annual pricing is published.

The main limitations are the lack of an ongoing free plan, per-user billing that scales costs with team size, and some inconsistency between the homepage and pricing page about exactly which tier includes computer use. Buyers should budget based on the credit tiers rather than a flat seat price.

Lindy suits teams who want an AI teammate that takes real actions across a large number of integrations and are comfortable with per-user, credit-based pricing. It's a poor fit for anyone who needs a genuinely free plan or wants a single fixed price regardless of team size.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'lindy' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET pros = ARRAY[$x$Connects to 1,000+ integrations plus MCP servers, so agents act across real tools rather than just chatting$x$, $x$Team plan includes model selection and computer use, letting agents drive a browser and reach apps without a clean API$x$, $x$7-day free trial includes $50 in credits and requires no credit card$x$, $x$Enterprise tier covers SSO, SCIM, HIPAA with a signed BAA, and audit logs for regulated teams$x$, $x$Credit tiers are published transparently, scaling from 3,000 to 1,750,000 credits per month$x$]::text[]
 WHERE slug = 'lindy' AND lang = 'en';

