UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Writesonic started life as an AI copywriting tool, but the current product is positioned as an AI Search Visibility Platform focused on generative engine optimization (GEO). The core job now is tracking where and how your brand shows up inside AI answers.

On self-serve plans, the platform tracks brand visibility across ChatGPT, Gemini and Google AI Overviews. Full coverage of all 8 AI platforms, including Perplexity, Claude, Grok and Copilot, is reserved for the custom Enterprise tier.

Key capabilities include a GEO tracking dashboard, an Action Center that flags missing prompts and citation opportunities and suggests what to do about them, a SEO & Content AI agent, an AI Article Writer for long-form content, and sentiment analysis of how your brand is described in AI responses (available from the Growth tier up).

On pricing, the official site lists Starter at $99/mo billed monthly or $79/mo billed annually, Basic at $249/mo billed monthly or $199/mo billed annually, Growth at $499/mo billed monthly or $399/mo billed annually (marked most popular), and a custom Enterprise tier. There is a free trial with no credit card required, but no ongoing free plan.

The entry point is far above Writesonic's old cheap copywriting plans, and the broadest AI-platform coverage is locked behind the Enterprise tier rather than available self-serve. Sentiment analysis and the full Action Center are also gated to higher tiers.

This platform suits SEO teams, agencies and marketers who care about brand visibility inside AI search and want writing plus tracking in one place. If you just need occasional cheap AI copy, the current pricing and GEO focus will feel like overkill.$x$
