UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Grok is xAI's conversational AI, integrated with X and available at grok.com. The current flagship is Grok 4.7, also reachable through the xAI API and offered inside third-party tools such as Cursor.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'grok' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Grok is the chat assistant built by xAI. It lives both inside X (formerly Twitter) and as a standalone product at grok.com, and it is known for a looser, more opinionated conversational style than most rivals, plus tight access to real-time posts on X. xAI's documentation and news pages now also carry the 'SpaceXAI' label alongside the Grok branding.

The current flagship, announced September 21, 2026, is Grok 4.7, which xAI describes as 'the most capable model we've built.' It carries a 500k-token context window and a May 2026 knowledge cutoff, and is available through the xAI API as model grok-4.7. Earlier API models grok-4.6 and grok-4.5 remain available with the same 500k context window. xAI has also launched Grok Build, a dedicated coding model (grok-build-0.1) with a 256k-token context window, and Grok Bot, described as AI teammates bundled with SuperGrok subscription tiers and with Cursor plans.

On capabilities, Grok handles text chat, image and video understanding, web and X search, and image/video generation through Grok Imagine. Developers can reach the chat and coding models through the xAI API, and Grok 4.7 is also offered through Cursor and through intermediaries such as OpenRouter, Vercel, and Cloudflare.

For the API, grok-4.7 is priced at $2.00 per million input tokens, $0.50 per million cached input tokens, and $6.00 per million output tokens for prompts under 200k tokens, rising to $4.00 / $1.00 / $12.00 above 200k tokens; a faster variant costs up to twice as much. The older grok-4.3 model is cheaper, at $1.25 input / $2.50 output per million tokens under 200k tokens, with a 1M-token context window. xAI also sells consumer subscriptions named SuperGrok, SuperGrok Plus, and SuperGrok Heavy, but their current prices are not published on xAI's open plan pages as of this writing. xAI's Grok 4.7 announcement states that Grok Build can be tried for free, but it is unclear whether the main Grok chat assistant still has a free tier.

The main limitation right now is that consumer pricing and the status of any free tier for Grok chat could not be confirmed from xAI's own plan pages, which return access errors or load only via JavaScript. The model lineup also iterates quickly, with 4.5, 4.6, and 4.7 all shipping within a few months of each other, so capabilities and pricing can change fast.

Grok suits developers who want API or Cursor access to xAI's models, people already active on X who want an assistant wired into live posts, and anyone who prefers a more candid, less filtered conversational style. Buyers should check xAI's own pricing pages directly before committing to a consumer plan, since current rates are not independently verifiable.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'grok' AND lang = 'en';

