UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Adobe Firefly is a generative AI creative studio for image, video, and audio, built on Adobe's own Firefly Image Model 5 (GA March 2026) alongside partner models from vendors such as Google, Runway, Kling, Luma, and ElevenLabs.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'adobe-firefly' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Adobe Firefly began as the AI generation engine inside Photoshop and Illustrator, but it has grown into a standalone creative studio on the web and in dedicated apps. It now spans image, video, and audio generation rather than just still images, and Adobe's own Firefly models keep the commercial-safe positioning Adobe built its reputation on.

The headline change is Firefly Image Model 5, Adobe's flagship image model, which reached general availability in March 2026. It generates natively at 4MP without a separate upscaling step, and Adobe reports improved photorealism and anatomy over earlier models, along with Prompt to Edit, a conversational way to edit an existing image, and custom style models.

Beyond Adobe's own models, Firefly now acts as an aggregator, hosting third-party models from vendors including Google, OpenAI, Black Forest Labs (FLUX), Runway, Kling, Luma, ElevenLabs, and Topaz. That lets you switch between Adobe and partner engines for image, video, and audio work inside one interface.

The free tier offers daily-refreshing free generations across image, video, and audio, with limits resetting each day; Adobe does not publish a fixed monthly credit number for this tier. Paid plans are billed per month: Firefly Standard at $9.99/month includes 2,000 premium credits, Firefly Pro at $19.99/month includes 4,000 premium credits, a newer Firefly Pro Plus tier at $49.99/month includes 10,000 premium credits, and Firefly Premium at $199.99/month includes 50,000 premium credits. On all paid tiers, standard image tools such as Text to Image and Generative Fill are unlimited, with credits spent only on premium features like video, audio, and partner models. Team plans are also available, billed annually.

The main limitation is the credit economy: premium credits for video, audio, and partner-model use can drain quickly even on paid plans, and the growing number of tiers (five consumer plans plus team options) adds pricing complexity. Adobe's commercially-safe guarantee applies to Adobe's own Firefly models, not necessarily to output from the third-party partner models hosted within the platform.

Firefly suits designers and content teams who want commercially safe generation from Adobe's own models, and anyone already inside Adobe's ecosystem who wants image, video, and audio plus multiple partner models under one subscription.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'adobe-firefly' AND lang = 'en';

