UPDATE tools SET description = $x$ComfyUI is an open-source, node-based visual editor for building image, video and other generative AI pipelines using diffusion models and partner API nodes, with new releases issued roughly weekly. It is available as a free self-hosted app or as the managed Comfy Cloud service for those who want GPU compute without local setup.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'comfyui' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$ComfyUI is a graph-based interface for running diffusion and other generative models. Instead of a single prompt box, you wire together nodes (loaders, samplers, conditioning, upscalers and more) into a workflow you can inspect, reuse and share. That transparency is why it became a go-to tool for people who want precise control over how an image or video is generated.

The project is actively maintained on GitHub (Comfy-Org/ComfyUI), with new releases issued roughly weekly covering reworked nodes, expanded model support and performance updates across GPU generations.

Beyond still images, ComfyUI can drive video, audio and other generation through open models and partner API nodes, including integrations from vendors such as Anthropic, Ideogram, HeyGen, Black Forest Labs and xAI, so it is no longer only an image tool. You can chain multiple models, mix custom and community nodes, batch-process, and export whole workflows as reusable JSON files.

Pricing has two sides. The self-hosted software is free and open source (GPL-3.0) via GitHub. The official Comfy Cloud managed service offers a one-off free trial of 5 GPU runs with no credit card required (no model import, 30-minute max runtime), then paid tiers billed monthly or at a discount annually: Standard at $20/month, Creator at $35/month (with model import from CivitAI and Hugging Face), Pro at $100/month, and Team at $700/month for up to 50 members with a shared credit pool, plus a custom Enterprise tier.

The main limitation is the learning curve: the node graph is powerful but intimidating for beginners, and running locally means managing GPU hardware, model files and dependencies yourself. Comfy Cloud removes the setup burden but ties usage to a metered credit budget and runtime caps that scale with the paid tier.

Choose ComfyUI if you want deep, reproducible control over generation, are comfortable with a technical interface, or want to start free locally and move to a managed cloud service later.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'comfyui' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET pros = ARRAY[$x$Free and fully open-source when self-hosted, with no feature paywall on the core app$x$, $x$Node graph gives precise, reproducible control and workflows are shareable as JSON$x$, $x$Covers image, video and other generative workflows, not just still images, via open models and partner API nodes$x$, $x$Actively maintained with frequent updates improving nodes, performance and GPU support$x$, $x$Optional Comfy Cloud, including a free trial of 5 GPU runs, removes local setup for those who want it$x$]::text[]
 WHERE slug = 'comfyui' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET cons = ARRAY[$x$Steep learning curve; the node interface is unintuitive for newcomers$x$, $x$Self-hosting requires capable GPU hardware plus manual model and dependency management$x$, $x$Comfy Cloud usage is metered by credits with capped runtime, which can limit heavy workloads$x$, $x$Quality of experience depends heavily on community custom nodes that vary in reliability$x$, $x$Comfy Cloud's free offering is a one-off trial of 5 runs, not a recurring monthly allowance$x$]::text[]
 WHERE slug = 'comfyui' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET choose_if = $x$["You want granular, reproducible control over generation pipelines", "You are comfortable with a technical, node-based interface", "You need image, video and other generation in one tool", "You prefer a free self-hosted setup but may want managed cloud later", "You want to build and share reusable JSON workflows"]$x$::jsonb
 WHERE slug = 'comfyui' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET faq = $x$[{"q": "What is ComfyUI?", "a": "ComfyUI is a node-based engine for running generative AI models across image, video, audio and 3D, using both open models and partner/API nodes, not just Stable Diffusion. Instead of simple form inputs, you build visual workflows by connecting nodes — model loaders, samplers, ControlNets, upscalers — into custom pipelines. It gives maximum control over every generation parameter."}, {"q": "Is ComfyUI better than Automatic1111?", "a": "ComfyUI is more powerful and faster but has a steeper learning curve. Automatic1111 (A1111) is more beginner-friendly with a familiar form-based interface. Most advanced users prefer ComfyUI for its flexibility and speed. Many use A1111 to learn and then switch to ComfyUI."}, {"q": "Do I need ComfyUI to use Stable Diffusion?", "a": "No. Stable Diffusion runs through multiple frontends: Automatic1111, ComfyUI, Fooocus, InvokeAI. ComfyUI is one option — it's the best for complex workflows but not required for basic generation. Fooocus is the simplest option; A1111 is the most documented."}]$x$::jsonb
 WHERE slug = 'comfyui' AND lang = 'en';

