UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Semrush is a marketing and SEO platform for keyword research, competitor analysis, site audits and content optimization. The current version, Semrush One (2026), adds an AI Visibility Toolkit that tracks how your brand shows up in ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity and Google AI Overviews.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'semrush' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Semrush is one of the longest-running online-visibility platforms, built around keyword research, rank tracking, backlink and traffic analysis, technical site audits and content tools. Marketers, agencies and SEO teams use it to size up competitors and plan campaigns across search and paid channels.

In 2026 the product was repositioned around AI search under the Semrush One plan family, which runs Free, SEO, Starter, Pro+, Advanced and a custom Enterprise tier. That same year Adobe completed its acquisition of Semrush, on April 28, 2026, for roughly $1.9 billion at $12 per share, and has since launched Adobe Brand Visibility, which combines Semrush with Adobe's own products.

The current toolkit bundles the classic SEO features with a new AI Visibility Toolkit that monitors brand mentions across ChatGPT, Gemini, Perplexity and Google AI Overviews, alongside a newer LLM Gap Analyzer app and Bot and Agent Analytics that show which AI crawlers are hitting your site.

On monthly billing the Semrush One tiers are $139/mo for SEO, $199/mo for Starter (which adds AI Visibility and 50 prompts/day), $299/mo for Pro+ and $549/mo for Advanced; paying annually lowers these to about $117.33, $165.17, $248.17 and $455.67 per month respectively. Enterprise pricing is custom, and additional user seats are billed separately starting at $45/mo. A free account (one demo project, 10 reports per day across the vital tools, no credit card) and a 7-day trial are also available.

The main drawbacks are cost and complexity: entry pricing is high for freelancers, extra seats and add-ons stack up quickly, and the breadth of tools and renamed plan tiers create a real learning curve. The most useful AI-visibility features sit on the Starter plan and above, not the base SEO tier.

Semrush fits agencies, in-house marketing teams and serious SEO practitioners who want one platform covering both traditional search rankings and the newer question of how a brand surfaces inside AI answers.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'semrush' AND lang = 'en';

