UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Pitch is an AI presentation workspace built around Pitch Agent, a conversational AI that generates fully on-brand decks from a prompt and your files, then rewrites, splits, and refines slides on request. It combines that agent with real-time collaboration and shared brand templates.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'pitch' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Pitch is a web-based tool for creating and collaborating on presentations. It started as a design-forward alternative to PowerPoint and Google Slides, aimed at teams that want polished decks without fighting with formatting.

As of October 2026, Pitch's homepage headline reads "Create slides that win," with Pitch Agent promoted as the way to generate on-brand slides. Instead of a simple AI writing helper, Pitch Agent is a conversational agent: you describe what you need and upload supporting files, and it drafts a complete presentation using your team's approved templates. You can then ask it to rewrite a section, break up an overcrowded slide, tighten the story, or answer questions about the deck itself.

The rest of the product still matters. Pitch keeps its shared brand templates so every deck stays consistent, live collaboration and comments for working with teammates, analytics on shared links, and a large library of starting layouts. The company reports serving more than 4 million teams.

Pricing is tiered. The free plan covers 1-5 members with 100 one-time AI credits, unlimited presentations, custom templates, and 2 external guests. Plus is a single-seat tier with monthly AI credits, custom fonts, video uploads, PPTX export, and 5 external guests. Team covers up to 25 members with a shared pool of monthly AI credits, multiple teamspaces, and 25 external guests. Business covers up to 200 members with a larger monthly AI credit pool and unlimited advanced links, teamspaces, and guests. Enterprise is custom-priced for 30+ seats and adds SAML SSO and a dedicated success manager. All paid tiers shown on the vendor's site are billed on an annual basis and priced in euros; annual billing saves roughly 17% versus month-to-month, though a verified USD monthly price could not be confirmed at review time.

The limits are worth noting. AI usage runs on monthly credits, so heavy Agent use can exhaust an allotment, and the Plus plan's credit pool covers only one seat. Pitch is presentation-only, so it will not replace a document or spreadsheet tool, and it is browser-first with no deep offline editing.

Pitch fits teams that produce a lot of branded decks and want AI drafting that respects their templates rather than generic slide output.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'pitch' AND lang = 'en';

