UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Nano Banana (nanobanana.io) is an independent AI image editing platform, not affiliated with Google, that offers character-consistent photo edits by routing requests to several third-party image and video models.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'nano-banana' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Nano Banana, at nanobanana.io, is an independent AI image generation and editing platform. Despite sharing its name with Google's own Nano Banana image models, the site states on its own pages that it has no affiliation with Google or any other product it references. It functions as a multi-model service, giving users access to several third-party models — including Seedream, GPT Image, Veo, Sora, Kling, Seedance and Qwen — through a single interface, rather than running a single proprietary model.

The platform is live and operating. Its core workflow is in-context editing: you upload a photo, describe the change in plain language, and the service applies the edit while aiming to preserve the original composition, lighting and scene structure, rather than generating an image from scratch.

Its headline feature is character consistency — keeping the same face, outfit or object recognizable across multiple edits or scenes, which the site markets toward serialized content creators, AI-influencer accounts and branded campaigns. Higher paid tiers add API access and support for multiple seats, aimed at teams rather than solo use.

Pricing is organized into Basic, Pro and Enterprise tiers, each billed annually, with credit allowances that scale with tier (roughly 15,000 credits/year on Basic up to 120,000 credits/year on Enterprise). The site also lists monthly and one-time purchase options, but those figures were not independently verified. New users receive a batch of free sign-in credits of unstated size before any purchase is required.

Because nanobanana.io is a reseller of outside models rather than Google's own Nano Banana (Gemini image models, available via the Gemini app, Google AI Studio and the Gemini API), its output quality and feature set depend on whichever underlying model it routes a given request to, and those models can change independent of this card. It suits creators who want a single interface for character-consistent editing without committing to one model vendor, but users who specifically want Google's Gemini image models should go directly to Google's own products.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'nano-banana' AND lang = 'en';

