UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Akkio is an AI workflow automation platform aimed at media agencies and data providers. Rather than a general-purpose dashboard tool, it packages its product around the stages of agency work, from strategy through to measurement.

The product has changed direction. Akkio started life as a no-code AI/ML tool for business analysts building forecasting models from CSV or CRM data. Its current homepage is titled 'The AI Workflow Automation Platform' and is explicitly aimed at media agencies and data providers, with a banner noting that Akkio is bringing AI infrastructure to retail media networks. There are no formal version numbers to track this shift.

The product is organized around five workflow stages: Strategize, Segment, Plan, Deploy and Measure. Named capabilities include Chat with Data for conversational analysis, no-code modeling, advanced reporting, and the ability to simulate multiple media plans before committing budget.

On pricing, the official site shows only a single Enterprise tier with custom, contact-sales pricing and no public figures. There is no free plan and no free trial listed on the official pricing page.

The main limitations are the narrowed focus and the pricing opacity. If you are not a media agency or data provider, the current product may be more than you need, and the move to contact-sales-only pricing makes it hard to gauge cost without a sales conversation. Some older agent or tool names associated with the product could not be confirmed on the current site.

Akkio suits media agencies and data providers that want to automate strategy, segmentation, planning, activation and measurement work, and enterprises comfortable with custom contracts. Analysts wanting a simple self-serve forecasting tool may find the product has moved past that use case.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'akkio' AND lang = 'en';

