UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Copy.ai is a GTM AI Platform (chat plus multi-step workflows and agents for sales, marketing and RevOps) built on OpenAI, Anthropic and Gemini models. There is no free plan; the entry tier is Chat at $29/mo.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'copy-ai' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Copy.ai started life as an AI copywriting assistant and has since repositioned itself as a "GTM AI Platform" aimed at go-to-market teams rather than individual writers. Instead of a single proprietary model, it routes work across leading third-party models from OpenAI, Anthropic and Google.

The product changed meaningfully in mid-2025. Copy.ai sunset its free plan along with the old Starter ($49) and Advanced ($249) writing tiers, and replaced the entry point with a flat, un-metered Chat plan at $29/mo. The site is now branded under Fullcast, with a Fullcast banner and Fullcast support email, which is consistent with heavier RevOps focus.

Core capabilities now split in two: a chat interface for everyday drafting (ads, emails, posts, briefs) and multi-step Workflows and agents that automate repetitive go-to-market tasks such as lead enrichment, account research and outbound sequences. The workflow layer is where the platform's real value sits.

Pricing has no free product tier. Chat is $29/mo (or $24/mo billed annually, $288/yr) with 5 seats and unlimited words. Team plans are billed annually: Growth is $1,000/mo billed annually ($12,000/yr, 75 seats, 20K workflow credits), Expansion is $2,000/mo billed annually ($24,000/yr, 150 seats, 45K credits) and Scale is $3,000/mo billed annually ($36,000/yr, 200 seats, 75K credits), with a custom Enterprise tier offering API access and 20+ integrations.

The main limitations are the pricing cliff between Chat and the team tiers, and the credit-metered workflows that can make heavier automation expensive to budget. Solo copywriters may also feel the tool has drifted away from them.

Copy.ai suits sales and marketing teams that want to automate go-to-market work with agents and workflows, and can justify team pricing. Individual writers who just want cheap copy generation have better-value options elsewhere.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'copy-ai' AND lang = 'en';

