UPDATE tools SET description = $x$Elicit is an AI research platform that searches across 138M+ academic papers and 545,000+ clinical trials, extracts structured data, and runs literature reviews. It now centers on the Elicit Research Agent and Routines, with an API and MCP server for integrating search and extraction into other tools.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'elicit' AND lang = 'en';

UPDATE tools SET description_long = $x$Elicit is a research intelligence platform built for academics, evidence synthesis teams, and anyone doing serious literature work. It searches a corpus of more than 138 million papers and 545,000 clinical trials, summarizes findings, lets you chat with papers, and pulls specific data points into structured tables.

The platform has moved well beyond simple paper search. Elicit introduced a public API and an MCP server in July 2026, launched the Elicit Research Agent in August 2026, and added Routines in September 2026, shifting the product from workflow-based limits to a monthly usage pool. The company's homepage currently states it is used by over 5 million researchers.

The core paid offering centers on systematic literature review and data extraction: you can screen thousands of papers, define custom extraction columns, and generate structured reports with sources you can verify.

Pricing is tiered. The Basic plan is free and includes unlimited search, unlimited summaries, unlimited chat-with-papers, source viewing, and Zotero import, with limited Research Agent and Reports usage. Pro is listed at $49 per user per month, billed annually ($588/year), and covers screening up to 5,000 papers, 20 extraction columns, and reports from up to 135 sources, plus API access. Scale is listed at $169 per user per month, billed annually ($2,028/year), with roughly 5x the usage of Pro, 30 columns, figure extraction, live collaboration, up to 200 sources, and admin controls. Enterprise is custom-priced and covers screening up to 40,000 papers, 40 columns, unlimited API access, and SSO/SAML/2FA. Standalone monthly-billing prices for Pro and Scale are not published on the pricing page.

Limitations are worth noting: the tool is tuned for academic and clinical literature rather than general web research, serious extraction and screening volumes require a paid plan, and as with any AI summarizer, extracted claims and citations still need human verification.

Elicit is a strong fit for researchers, PhD students, systematic reviewers, and R&D or clinical teams who need to move quickly through large bodies of evidence without losing the ability to trace every claim back to its source.$x$
 WHERE slug = 'elicit' AND lang = 'en';

