UPDATE tools SET faq = $x$[{"q": "What is Meta AI?", "a": "Meta AI is Meta's assistant built into WhatsApp, Instagram, Facebook, Messenger and Threads, plus Meta's AI glasses. As of April 2026 it runs on Muse Spark, Meta Superintelligence Labs' first proprietary model. It can answer questions, draft and rewrite text, summarize threads, and help in group chats, all without leaving Meta's apps. It remains free for everyday use, alongside optional paid Meta One plans."}, {"q": "Is Meta AI free?", "a": "Yes, Meta states the core Meta AI experience remains free for everyday use. On September 15, 2026, Meta also launched Meta One worldwide, a subscription system for extra usage of compute-heavy features. It includes single-app Plus plans (WhatsApp, Instagram, Facebook) and multi-app bundles: Core and Premium for consumers, and Essential, Advanced, Expert and Max for businesses and creators. Meta's published prices are in euros; US-dollar figures are not officially confirmed."}, {"q": "Is Meta AI as good as ChatGPT?", "a": "Meta AI now runs on Muse Spark, Meta Superintelligence Labs' first proprietary model, replacing the earlier Llama-based engine. It's built for everyday conversation, drafting and summarizing directly inside Meta's apps, which makes it convenient if you already live in WhatsApp, Instagram or Messenger. There's no official benchmark comparison to other assistants in the current description, so it's best evaluated on convenience and integration rather than raw model performance."}, {"q": "What is Muse?", "a": "Muse is a separate personal AI agent app that Meta launched in September 2026, powered by the same Muse Spark model as Meta AI. It is available at muse.ai and through WhatsApp, currently rolling out in the US, and is distinct from the Meta AI assistant built into Meta's main apps."}]$x$::jsonb
